Description: Fix overlapping widgets in the Preferences dialog's notebook pages
 dlgPreferences builds each notebook page's content by calling
 mainSizer.Fit(panel) *before* panel.SetSizer(mainSizer). For a plain
 top-level window this ordering is (surprisingly) harmless under
 current wxWidgets, but for a panel that becomes a wx.Notebook page,
 no further resize/layout event ever arrives to trigger the newly
 attached sizer's layout pass, since the page was already added to
 the notebook and sized before SetSizer() enables auto-layout on
 resize. The result: every child widget stays at its default creation
 position, (0, 0), rather than being stacked by the sizer.
 .
 Confirmed directly by instantiating the dialog and reading widget
 positions:
 .
   StaticText 'mMass can use your internet connection...' (0, 0) (378, 36)
   CheckBox 'Automatically check for updates' (0, 0) (243, 22)
   Button 'Check Now' (0, 0) (100, 34)
 .
 All three sat exactly on top of each other, which is what the user
 saw as garbled overlapping text and a misplaced button on the
 Software Updates page.
 .
 Fix: call panel.SetSizer() before Fit(), and add an explicit
 panel.Layout() call to force a layout pass regardless of event
 timing. After the fix the same widgets report distinct, correctly
 stacked positions ((10,10), (77,66), (149,108)). Applied to both
 notebook pages (makeUpdatesPage and the Windows-only
 makeCompassPanel, which has the identical structure and would hit
 the same bug, though it could not be tested directly on Linux).
